# Format / lint before the CI gate

Most `ci:check` failures here are **Prettier** (`format:check`) or easy **ESLint**
nits. Fix them on **touched paths** once, immediately **before**
`npm run ci:check` — not after every single edit (that wastes time re-running
the same files).

## When to run

1. Edit freely during the task (still aim for project style — see Prettier table).
2. When about to run `ci:check`, hand off, or commit: collect paths you changed
   this session (or `git diff --name-only` / staged names for that work).
3. Run Prettier (+ scoped ESLint if needed) on **those paths once**.
4. Then `npm run ci:check`.

Do **not** re-run Prettier/ESLint after every `Write`/`StrReplace` on the same
file. Mid-task format is optional only if you are done with that file for good
and will not touch it again before the gate.

## Project Prettier (`.prettierrc.json`)

| Option | Value |
| ------ | ----- |
| `singleQuote` | `true` |
| `trailingComma` | `"all"` |
| `printWidth` | `100` |
| `semi` | `true` |

Prefer single quotes, trailing commas where valid, semicolons, wrap near 100 cols.
Prettier on disk remains the source of truth.

## Commands (scoped to touched files)

```bash
npx prettier --write <path1> <path2> ...
npx eslint --fix <path1> <path2> ...   # only if ESLint-relevant; not a logic substitute
```

Avoid `npm run format` / `npm run lint:fix` on the **whole** tree unless the
user asked or many unrelated files are dirty.

## Relation to `ci:check`

```text
edits… → prettier --write (touched) → eslint --fix (touched, if needed) → npm run ci:check
```

- Do not burn review-fix rounds on format-only failures — format touched files
  first, then one `ci:check`.
- See also `ci-check-before-done`.
